      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can differentiate between pure fatigue and neurological hurdles by monitoring performance metrics relative to sport demands, such as a randomized regression or failure to exceed Existing expectations for performance on all types. If the athlete fails to perform key performance standards, it suggests either insufficient energy availability or neural adaptation beyond simple recovery. To confirm, consider testing peripheral blood markers for inflammation or neutrophil-lymphocyte ratios, which may indicate systemic strain versus central nervous system specific adaptation. Addressing either via targeted nutrition, periodized rest, or adjusted stimulus should clarify the root cause and guide your next programming step.",
