      "content": "Yes, psychological stressors like anxiety or performance pressure can indeed act as hidden brakes by increasing cortisol levels, which inhibits muscle protein synthesis. Environmental stressors such as new competition schedules, travel disruptions, or even suboptimal sleep environments can compound this effect, mimicking a physiological block. To address this invisible wall, perhaps consider integrating more active recovery days, reducing high-stress stimuli, or consulting a sports psychologist to rule out mental barriers to training.",
